  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Paragon Systems has received $342M in contract obligations in FY2026 to date across 254 awards, with an average award size of $1.3M. Paragon Systems obligations fell 42.8% year over year. Department of Homeland Security is the largest buyer, obligating $279M to Paragon Systems so far this year. Security Guards and Patrol Services is the largest market for Paragon Systems at $302M, followed by Security Systems Services (except Locksmiths) at $40.1M. Historical annual obligations show fluctuations: FY21 $634M, FY22 $595M, FY23 $669M, FY24 $617M, and FY25 $598M. Paragon Systems obligations in FY2026 to date are a partial fiscal-year total and represent the current-year snapshot of buying patterns and market concentration for the company.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "How concentrated are Paragon Systems obligations this year?",
        "body": "Department of Homeland Security accounted for the bulk of Paragon Systems obligations in FY2026 to date at $279M. Security Guards and Patrol Services accounted for the bulk of industry spending for Paragon Systems at $302M. Department of Health and Human Services, Department of Justice, National Archives and Records Administration, and Department of Defense together account for the remaining named agency obligations: $38.4M, $23M, $1.2M, and $820K respectively."
      },
      {
        "heading": "How does FY2026 to date compare with prior years for Paragon Systems?",
        "body": "Paragon Systems obligations in FY2026 to date are $342M compared with prior fiscal-year totals of FY21 $634M, FY22 $595M, FY23 $669M, FY24 $617M, and FY25 $598M. Paragon Systems obligations fell 42.8% year over year. Paragon Systems award count this year is 254 with an average award size of $1.3M."
      }
    ]
  },
